# Company Domain Specification

Version: 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Company Domain manages organisations participating in global trade.

A company is the central entity within ExportIQ.

Everything else in the platform ultimately relates to a company.

Examples include:

- Buyer
- Supplier
- Manufacturer
- Distributor
- Retailer
- Brand Owner

---

# Scope

The Company Domain is responsible for:

- Company identity
- Company lifecycle
- Company status
- Company relationships
- Company verification
- Company discoverability

The Company Domain is NOT responsible for:

- AI analysis
- Products
- Certifications
- Contacts
- Trade history

These belong to their respective domains.

---

# Business Definition

A company represents a legal organisation.

A company may perform multiple business roles.

A company may operate in multiple countries.

A company may trade multiple products.

A company exists independently of any role.

---

# Golden Record

Every company has exactly one Golden Record.

The Golden Record contains only verified business facts.

Examples

✓ Name

✓ Website

✓ Country

✓ Headquarters

✓ Status

✓ Legal Name

The Golden Record never stores:

✗ AI summaries

✗ AI recommendations

✗ Buyer score

✗ Opportunity score

✗ Risk analysis

Those belong to the AI Domain.

---

# Company Identity

Every company has two identifiers.

Internal Identifier

- UUID

External Identifier

- Company Code
- Example:
  CMP-000001

The Company Code is immutable.

---

# Company Lifecycle

DISCOVERED

↓

IDENTIFIED

↓

ENRICHED

↓

VERIFIED

↓

ACTIVE

↓

DORMANT

↓

ARCHIVED

A company may move forwards or backwards depending on new evidence.

---

# Verification

A company becomes verified when one or more trusted sources confirm its existence.

Verification sources include:

- Government Registry
- Company Website
- Human Review
- Trusted Data Provider

---

# Duplicate Detection

A new company candidate is compared using:

1. Website Domain

2. Registration Number (future)

3. Email Domain

4. Company Name + Country

5. AI Similarity

Duplicate resolution should preserve all evidence.

